
--- testing tag of simple choice type: ---

0
1
2
3
tag is 0 for choice choice bool i64 u8 String.0 NYI NYI
tag is 1 for choice choice bool i64 u8 String.1 NYI NYI
tag is 2 for choice choice bool i64 u8 String.2 NYI NYI
tag is 3 for choice choice bool i64 u8 String.3 NYI NYI

--- testing tags of some common choice types: ---

true .tag: 1 true expecting 1
false.tag: 0 false expecting 0
option String 'bla' .tag: 0 bla expecting 0
option String nil   .tag: 1 --nil-- expecting 1
option i64 42  .tag: 0 42 expecting 0
option i64 nil .tag: 1 --nil-- expecting 1

--- testing tags choice with several `void` entries: ---

id (choice unit void void) unit .tag 0 expecting 0
id (choice void unit void) unit .tag 1 expecting 1
id (choice void void unit) unit .tag 2 expecting 2
id (choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void) 42   .tag: 3 choice choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void.3 NYI NYI expecting 3
id (choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void) unit .tag: 6 choice choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void.6 NYI NYI expecting 6
id (choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void) nil  .tag: 7 choice choice void void void i32 void void unit nil void void.7 NYI NYI expecting 7

--- testing `option nil`, which is effectively `choice nil nil`, but it can have tags 0 and 1: ---

id (Sequence nil) [nil] .first.tag: 0 expecting 0
id (Sequence nil) []    .first.tag: 1 expecting 1

--- choice of unit types and ref types only are encoded using not tag field but special ref values by the C backend: ---

id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) unit    .tag 0 expecting 0
id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) 'str'   .tag 1 expecting 1
id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) nil     .tag 2 expecting 2
id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) [1,2,4] .tag 3 expecting 3
id (choice unit String nil (Sequence i64) concur) concur  .tag 4 expecting 4

--- choice of only unit types are treated like an int type by the JVM backend: ---

id (choice unit nil concur) unit   .tag 0 expecting 0
id (choice unit nil concur) nil    .tag 1 expecting 1
id (choice unit nil concur) concur .tag 2 expecting 2

--- testing with void alternatives ---

nil: 1 expecting 1

--- mix of void, several ref and several unit types ---

----blub----
1: StringYeahYeah!
2: nil
3: Sequence [1, 2, 3, 4]
4: unit

--- mix of void, one ref type, choice type and several unit types ---

----blob----
1: StringYeahYeah!
2: nil
3: option Sequence [1, 2, 3, 4]
4: unit
